{
  "$comment": "Chapter 4 level 37. Idea: every stage you finish wakes another wolf pack, and the woods close in as you push north. A wooded upland: the player clearing in the south, the turtle rival on a hill walled by cliffs in the north (disc aboveSea 100, falloff 2) that no army can climb until objective 3, when five shape steps raise a stone ramp on its south face, so the rival lives until its stage. Stage 1 clear the 5 wolf den in the birch wood 32 cells east (raids of 4 wardens from minute 10, every 120 s, until 0, so an idle village falls near tick 14000). Stage 2 the dormant old shrine wakes (4 followers, 90 s, teaches the Fire Lodge); a pack of 4 wakes in the bracken beside it when your people reach the glade. Stage 3 the prayer wakes two packs of 7 (southwest hollow and northeast thicket); clear any two dens from this stage on (clearDens fromStage n 2 without an area, because the validator counts only setup dens in an area; the far west den is the second setup den). Stage 4 a pack wakes in the fern hollow and a war band (10 wardens, 2 firecallers) climbs down 45 s later, then 4 wardens every 100 s until 12 are cut down. Stage 5 the ramp rises, a pack of 5 wakes at its foot, and the rival musters 4 wardens on its walls 30, 90, 150 and 210 s later (16 wardens, 6 firecallers posted, 3 towers, maxTroops 12, maxPopulation 30). Every raid and muster is warned 10 s before. Measured with the hard aggressive bot at offset 1: stages done near ticks 4512, 6962, 7922, 9137, 16717 (offsets 0 to 3 win between about 15750 and 17000). Time limit 2000 s (40000 ticks).",
